From: MrlingXD <90316914+wling-art@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 08:40:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Leaf: Skip unused delayed leash holder lookups

Only resolve a nonzero delayed leash holder ID on the client. Retain the existing resolution and current-holder return behavior.

Original patch: https://github.com/Winds-Studio/Leaf/blob/06c9c91a17e61aeed16bcfc846ebe91aa70d6c84/leaf-server/minecraft-patches/features/0287-Optimize-getLeashHolder.patch

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/entity/Leashable.java b/net/minecraft/world/entity/Leashable.java
index 8bec3de958e129e25955459cccfa1e8f9ec059d1..2321aa34ce1271692335cedd4b7452ac7ed75916 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/entity/Leashable.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/entity/Leashable.java
@@ -372,10 +372,15 @@ public interface Leashable {
             return null;
         }
 
-        Entity ntt = entity.level().getEntity(leashData.delayedLeashHolderId);
-        if (leashData.delayedLeashHolderId != 0 && entity.level().isClientSide() && ntt != null) {
-            leashData.setLeashHolder(ntt);
+        // Leaf start - Optimize getLeashHolder - only resolve delayed leash holders on the client
+        final Level level = entity.level();
+        if (leashData.delayedLeashHolderId != 0 && level.isClientSide()) {
+            final Entity holder = level.getEntity(leashData.delayedLeashHolderId);
+            if (holder != null) {
+                leashData.setLeashHolder(holder);
+            }
         }
+        // Leaf end - Optimize getLeashHolder
 
         return leashData.leashHolder;
     }
